package "main"

// A struct that contains ITSELF by value (`type C struct { self C }`, or through
// an array field `{ items [2]C }`, or a mutual cycle `A{b B}; B{a A}`) has no
// finite layout.  collectTypeDecl used to leave the cyclic Underlying in place, so
// the size / destruction / ABI walks that recurse through by-value fields
// stack-overflowed the compiler (SIGSEGV at compile time).  It now rejects the
// definition and breaks the cycle (poisoning the offending field), so the walks
// terminate.  A cycle through a POINTER (`@C` / `*C`) is a valid recursive type
// (linked-list node) and stays legal.

type C struct {
	self C
}

func main() {
	println(0)
}
